      <slug></slug>
      <title>Mono C++ Interop</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Mono devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Mono C++ Interop&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;One of Mono&amp;#39;s long-standing limitations is C++ interoperability, or&#xA;lack thereof. This talk will focus on a new framework, developed&#xA;during Google Summer of Code by Alex Corrado, that adds C++ Interop&#xA;support to Mono with no native glue code. We will look at what&amp;#39;s&#xA;supported now, what it can do, how C++ libraries can be bound, what&#xA;work is still needed and what the future holds for C++ on Mono.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2001">Andreia Gaita</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>